BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) runs this r
 esidency with Videotage\, a Hong Kong-based non-profit media arts institut
 ion specialising in the promotion\, presentation\, creation and preservati
 on of moving image and media art in all forms and languages. The Fund is r
 ecruiting one Netherlands-based designer\, maker or observer working in di
 gital culture to spend two or three months at Videotage's studio space in 
 Hong Kong in 2027\, conducting research\, broadening their network\, devel
 oping new work inspired by Hong Kong\, and presenting their findings or co
 mpleted works. The residency encourages crossovers and experimentation\, g
 iving the participant space to explore new methodologies\, widen their cre
 ative practice and produce work that pushes the boundaries of digital cult
 ure\, with a focus on social and urban dynamics. The 2027 edition takes th
 e technological 'black box' phenomenon as its starting point and invites t
 he resident to respond to that theme within the context of Videotage. ELIG
 IBILITY: you are an individual designer\, maker or observer within the fie
 ld of digital culture\; you are established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, B
 onaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the N
 etherlands)\; you are registered in the business register of the Dutch Cha
 mber of Commerce (KvK) or another business register within the Kingdom of 
 the Netherlands\; and you have had a professional practice in the creative
  industry for at least four years. NOT open to duos\, collectives or coope
 rative ventures\, nor to designers and makers who receive a grant during t
 he work period under the Talent Development Grant Scheme\, the Open Call S
 elf-taught Designer or the Open Call Emerging Design Practices ABCSSS. Not
 e that accepting this open call means you cannot apply to those schemes an
 d open calls in 2027. FUNDING: EUR 5\,000 for two months or EUR 6\,500 for
  three months\, covering travel\, insurance\, living expenses\, compensati
 on for time invested and material and transport costs\; accommodation\, st
 udio use and Videotage's facilitation are covered separately by the Fund. 
 Submit your proposal to the Creative Industries Fund NL by 21 October 2026
 \, 16:00 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Cre
 ative Industries Fund NL) in collaboration with Videotage\, Hong Kong\nLoc
 ation: Residency takes place at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must be
  established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint 
 Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a
  business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 5\,0
 00 for a two-month residency or EUR 6\,500 for a three-month residency\, p
 aid by the Creative Industries Fund NL to cover travel\, insurance\, livin
 g expenses\, compensation for time invested\, and material and transport c
 osts. Accommodation\, use of the studio space and facilitation by Videotag
 e are covered directly by the Fund on top of this. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Two or three months in 2027 (spring 2027)\; state your preferred p
 eriod in the application.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/gra
 nts/open-call-videotage?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must b
 e established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint
  Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in 
 a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-delfina-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Delfina Foundation Residency 2027 (London
 )
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at London's Delfina Fou
 ndation\, one of the UK's best known artist-in-residence programmes\, hous
 ed at 29-31 Catherine Place near Buckingham Palace with space for 6 to 8 i
 nternational residents (own room\, shared kitchen and facilities). Delfina
  promotes artistic exchange and experiment\, offering visual artists and c
 urators a platform to carry out research\, develop ideas and position thei
 r practice within the global discourse\, with introductions to the London 
 art scene and Delfina's international network. The programme includes visi
 ts to museums\, galleries and non-profit platforms\, discussions with Lond
 on-based artists\, portfolio reviews with curators and regular networking 
 lunches\; residents are expected to take part. Applicants are not asked fo
 r a concrete project proposal but must submit a clear motivation: why they
  wish to take part\, what research they want to conduct\, and how it can c
 ontribute to Delfina's ongoing programme. WHO: visual artists and curators
  based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; duo appli
 cations not possible\; application must be in English. One work period ava
 ilable: 27 September to 17 December 2027. Selection by an advisory committ
 ee with a Delfina representative\; processing may exceed three months. DEA
 DLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00 Dutch time / 11:00 Caribbean
  time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Delfina Foundation\nLocation: Lon
 don\, UK. For visual artists and curators based in the Netherlands or the 
 Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.\nAward: Subs
 idy of EUR 9\,188 for an artist or EUR 7\,232 for a curator/art observer t
 oward travel\, material and living costs (a 10 percent personal contributi
 on is automatically deducted by the Mondriaan Fund)\; studio\, living spac
 e and Delfina Foundation support are paid directly by the Mondriaan Fund. 
 Contribution for Caribbean-based artists can be increased for higher trave
 l costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: 27 September to 17 D
 ecember 2027\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/g
 rants/residency/delfina-foundation-londen-uk/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/del
 fina-foundation-londen-uk/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:London\, UK. For visual artists and curators based in the Netherla
 nds or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-inside-out-art-museum-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Inside-Out Art Museum Residency 2027 (Bei
 jing)
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at Inside-Out Art Museu
 m (IOAM) in Beijing\, one of China's leading independent platforms for con
 temporary art and research. The museum combines exhibitions\, critical inq
 uiry and public programmes\, giving residents room for in-depth research\,
  experimentation and exchange within a Chinese art scene that is otherwise
  hard to access from Europe. The residency is framed as cultural exchange 
 rather than production to deadline: IOAM works with a flexible model that 
 takes the resident's other obligations into account and sets the exact sta
 rt date in consultation with the selected candidate. WHO: visual artists\,
  curators and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of th
 e Kingdom. Duos and collaborations may apply (two artists\, two curators/c
 ritics\, or a combination who structurally make work together\, submitting
  a joint plan for the work period that leads to a single result\, and who 
 live and work together in the same space during the residency)\, but each 
 individual must submit a separate application\; the apartment is well suit
 ed to duos or partnerships. WORK PERIOD: one period of three months\, 1 Ma
 rch to 30 May 2027\, with room for one artist or duo\; you can state a pre
 ference for the work period in the application form. Selection is by advis
 ory committee\; read the Mondriaan Fund Residency explanation for the cond
 itions\, assessment and checklist\, plus the fund's general terms and cond
 itions\, before applying. DEADLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00
  Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Insi
 de-Out Art Museum\nLocation: Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curator
 s and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdo
 m\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.\nAward: Subsidy of EUR 8\,478 for an art
 ist or EUR 5\,622 for a curator/critic toward travel\, material and living
  costs (a 10 percent personal contribution is automatically deducted by th
 e Mondriaan Fund)\; studio\, living space and Inside-Out Art Museum suppor
 t are paid directly by the Mondriaan Fund. For a selected duo the total is
  increased proportionally to cover the second applicant's travel and accom
 modation. Contribution for Caribbean-based residents can be increased for 
 higher travel costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: 1 March 
 to 30 May 2027 (flexible start date\, set by IOAM in consultation with the
  resident)\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regel
 ingen/residency/inside-out-art-museum-beijing-china/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regelingen/residency/i
 nside-out-art-museum-beijing-china/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curators and critics based i
 n the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mon
 driaan Fund.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stichting-stokroos-residency-fundaziun-nairs-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260911
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260912
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Residency at Fundaziun Nairs 2026
DESCRIPTION:Stichting Stokroos funds a three-month reflective residency at 
 Fundaziun Nairs in Scuol\, Switzerland\, for one selected visual artist\, 
 designer or craft practitioner (overlap possible). Both emerging and estab
 lished makers may apply. Stokroos covers full accommodation and meals dire
 ctly with Fundaziun Nairs and provides a discretionary EUR 7\,000 budget f
 or living\, travel and production. The application should include a propos
 al that engages specifically with the residency\, its Alpine surroundings 
 and/or its historical and cultural context. Eligibility: you completed you
 r first subject-specific (vocational or higher) programme in 2022 or earli
 er\, or have an equivalent established practice\, or started without forma
 l training (first presentation marks the start of your practice)\; at leas
 t 21 years old\; living and working in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (inc
 luding its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; not curren
 tly enrolled in a study or post-academic programme. Applications are indiv
 idual only\; duos and collectives cannot apply. Makers already selected by
  Fundaziun Nairs may still apply if they meet the criteria. You may submit
  only one application per year across all Stokroos grants\, and must not h
 ave received a Seed Grant rejection in the previous calendar year. Apply v
 ia the online form (Dutch or English) with a portfolio PDF up to 20 pages\
 , optional video up to 10 minutes total\, CV up to 2 pages\, and work/plan
  descriptions up to 2\,500 characters each. Selection includes an introduc
 tory interview with up to three candidates\; Stokroos aims to respond with
 in 8 weeks. No appeal is possible. Application window: 1 to 11 September 2
 026. More information at nairs.ch.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting Stokroos\nLo
 cation: Residency in Scuol\, Switzerland (Fundaziun Nairs). Applicants mus
 t live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname for at least one year. Applicants outside the Randstad
  particularly encouraged.\nAward: Fully supported stay (accommodation and 
 meals paid directly to Fundaziun Nairs) plus an unrestricted living\, trav
 el and production budget of EUR 7\,000. 80% paid before the residency\, th
 e remainder on receipt of a brief final report. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Intensive three-month working period (July through September).\n\nMor
 e: https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-residency-fundaziun-nairs
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-residency-fundaziun-nairs
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency in Scuol\, Switzerland (Fundaziun Nairs). Applicants mus
 t live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname for at least one year. Applicants outside the Randstad
  particularly encouraged.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kb-researcher-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:Deadline: KB Researcher-in-Residence (RiR) 2027
DESCRIPTION:ELIGIBILITY: two Researcher-in-Residence positions in 2027. Ope
 n to early-career researchers of any discipline (data science\, social sci
 ence\, computer science\, humanities) who are currently working on a PhD o
 r within 5 years of their PhD end date. You must have\, or be able to secu
 re\, an affiliation with a Dutch university or research institute willing 
 to second you\; external PhD students may use the funding to obtain such a
  contract. Your project must make use of one or more of the KB digital col
 lections and you must be able to work with primarily Dutch data. You must 
 be available at 0.5 FTE over 6 months and able to spend two days a week on
 -site at the KB in The Hague. COLLECTIONS: over 130 million digitized page
 s of newspapers\, magazines\, radio bulletins and books from 1470 onward (
 via Delpher and DBNL)\, a born-digital web collection of more than 23\,000
  websites\, ground-truth and derived datasets on the KB Lab\, and metadata
  including Linked Data. APPLY: use the official proposal template and subm
 it a single PDF by 27 September 2026 to dh@kb.nl\, after reading the call'
 s terms and conditions\; questions to dh@kb.nl. TIMELINE: deadline 27 Sept
 ember 2026\; internal eligibility review followed by an external committee
  review\; outcome notified November 2026\; residencies start Q1 and Q3 202
 7. DISCIPLINES: digital humanities / data science / computational research
  with cultural-heritage collections. NOTE: the output is usually a dataset
  or tool prototype hosted on the KB Lab\; you agree to share results via b
 log posts on the KB Lab and to publish resulting tools or data under an op
 en license within 6 months of the residency. Proposals should align with t
 he KB Research Agenda or the Cultural AI Lab.\n\nOrganisation: KB\, Nation
 al Library of the Netherlands\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands (two days
  per week on-site at the KB premises)\nAward: Secondment at 0.5 FTE for 6 
 months based on your current salary\, up to EUR 5\,590 gross per month for
  a full-time-equivalent position\, plus travel expenses\, office facilitie
 s\, and support from a research software engineer\, research advisor\, and
  collection and data specialists. No application fee.\nDuration: 6 months 
 at 0.5 FTE (two days per week on-site)\; two positions in 2027\, starting 
 Q1 and Q3\n\nMore: https://lab.kb.nl/news/call-kb-researcher-residence-rir
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://lab.kb.nl/news/call-kb-researcher-residence-rir-2027?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands (two days per week on-site at the KB premi
 ses)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Residency
DESCRIPTION:The Mondriaan Fund's Residency grant supports professional visu
 al artists\, curators\, and art observers who want to deepen their practic
 e through a residency in the Netherlands or abroad. It contributes to the 
 costs of a self-arranged residency that offers meaningful development for 
 the applicant's work. WHO CAN APPLY: visual artists\, curators\, and art o
 bservers who have been professionally active for at least one year and are
  based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. AMOUNT: th
 e grant amount varies depending on the residency's location and duration\;
  applicants must contribute at least 10% of the costs themselves\, through
  personal investment\, third-party contributions\, an interest-free loan\,
  or crowdfunding. APPLYING: submitted through the Mondriaan Fund's online 
 application portal\, which requires a pre-created account (allow several w
 orking days). DEADLINE: 27 August 2026\, 16:00 Dutch time (11:00 Caribbean
  time).\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund (Mondriaan Fonds)\nLocation: Nethe
 rlands. Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part 
 of the Kingdom\; residencies may take place in the Netherlands or abroad.\
 nAward: Grant amount varies depending on the location and duration of the 
 residency. Applicants must contribute at least 10% themselves (personal in
 vestment\, third-party contributions\, an interest-free loan\, or crowdfun
 ding).\nDuration: Varies by residency.\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds
 .nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Ca
 ribbean part of the Kingdom\; residencies may take place in the Netherland
 s or abroad.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:futures-of-listening-earth-immersion-trembling-planet-2027@artificialno
 uveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: Futures of Listening x KNMI: Earth Immersion\, Trembling 
 Planet Residency
DESCRIPTION:One residency for an artist\, designer or maker working with so
 und\, exploring spatial sound in relation to seismology\, climate and disc
 harge-related acoustics\, run with the Royal Netherlands Meteorological In
 stitute. THE PREMISE: climate change is making major landslides\, ice-brea
 koff events from marine-terminating glaciers\, and sound-producing ice mov
 ements more common. These generate infrasonic vibrations inaudible to huma
 ns that sometimes spread across the entire planet and into the atmosphere.
  The residency asks how immersive sound techniques can make these events t
 angible and build meaningful sonic narratives from them. WHAT YOU GET ACCE
 SS TO: scientific data on seismological events\, vibrations\, infrasound a
 nd the movement of land and ice masses\, with scientific expertise from KN
 MI (lead researcher Jelle Assink) and artistic guidance from the Futures o
 f Listening team\, relating local events to global impact. RESEARCH QUESTI
 ONS to position your proposal against include how immersive sound can cult
 ivate situated listening to ecological processes and more-than-human encou
 nters\, how artistic and scientific methods of working with environmental 
 data can inform each other\, and what is gained\, lost or ethically at sta
 ke when environmental sounds are translated\, interpreted or reconstructed
  through spatial and synthetic means. DELIVERABLE: residents are expected 
 to create a final spatial sound production using the 4DSOUND system. Other
  outcomes may include immersive installations\, data-driven sonic works\, 
 audiovisual pieces\, software prototypes or reusable methodologies. Experi
 ence in art-science environments is welcome but not required\; you may ins
 tead explain why working in one would benefit your practice. HARD ELIGIBIL
 ITY GATE: applicants must be based in the Netherlands AND registered as an
  artist with the Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK). This is not negotiable a
 nd rules out non-NL applicants. Futures of Listening is a Netherlands-base
 d platform for spatial sound\, immersive experience\, performance and inst
 allation art\, founded by FIBER Festival\, 4DSOUND\, Robin Koek and Art of
  Sound at the Royal Conservatoire The Hague\, supported by CIIIC and Stimu
 leringsfonds.\n\nOrganisation: Futures of Listening (FIBER\, 4DSOUND\, Rob
 in Koek\, Art of Sound) in collaboration with KNMI\, the Royal Netherlands
  Meteorological Institute\nLocation: Partially self-hosted\, partially at 
 the 4DSOUND studio in Amsterdam\, and partially at KNMI in De Bilt near Ut
 recht\, Netherlands.\nAward: Total residency fee of EUR 7\,125\, calculate
 d as 25 commissioned days at a day rate of EUR 285. Six of those 25 days c
 an be spent at the 4DSOUND studio working with their team. Some additional
  financial support is available if needed\, including material and travel 
 costs\, but these must be clearly defined and agreed before the residency 
 starts. No application fee.\nDuration: January to March 2027\, structured 
 as 25 commissioned days. Deadline 13 September 2026.\n\nMore: https://fibe
 r.homerun.co/artist-residency-earth-immersion/en?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fiber.homerun.co/artist-residency-earth-immersion/en?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Partially self-hosted\, partially at the 4DSOUND studio in Amsterd
 am\, and partially at KNMI in De Bilt near Utrecht\, Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:futures-of-listening-architecture-on-sound-2027@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: Futures of Listening: Architecture on Sound Residency
DESCRIPTION:One residency for an individual practitioner\, a duo or a studi
 o working at the intersection of sound and space\, exploring architecture 
 through spatial audio. THE PREMISE: architecture is traditionally conceive
 d through form\, structure\, material and light\, with sound treated as so
 mething to be controlled or optimised afterwards. This residency asks what
  happens if architecture begins with sound\, shifting the question from ho
 w a space should sound to how sound can generate space. Spatial audio\, vi
 rtual acoustics and immersive media now allow prototyping of responsive en
 vironments\, impossible architectures and sonic spaces beyond physical con
 straints. RESEARCH QUESTIONS include how sound can become a first principl
 e in architectural and spatial design\, how the acoustic properties of spa
 ce inform the creation and perception of spatial sound\, and how artistic 
 research can shape the future tools\, interfaces and methods of spatial so
 und creation. NOT JUST ARTWORKS: they explicitly say they want new methods
 \, insights and creative infrastructures too. Outcomes may include install
 ations\, spatial audio compositions\, performances\, audiovisual works\, s
 oftware prototypes\, reusable methodologies or modular interfaces. Residen
 ts may collaborate with a 4DSOUND software developer to prototype new tool
 s\, and practitioners who already build their own software\, hardware or c
 reative technologies are encouraged to advance those as part of the reside
 ncy. WHO: architects are the named invitees\, with scenographers\, spatial
  designers\, installation artists\, sound artists\, composers and creative
  technologists also encouraged. Creative coding experience is welcome but 
 not required. Lead researcher is Poul Holleman\, co-founder and director o
 f 4DSOUND. HARD ELIGIBILITY GATE: applicants must be based in the Netherla
 nds AND registered as an artist with the Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK). 
 This is not negotiable and rules out non-NL applicants. Futures of Listeni
 ng is a Netherlands-based platform for spatial sound\, immersive experienc
 e\, performance and installation art\, founded by FIBER Festival\, 4DSOUND
 \, Robin Koek and Art of Sound at the Royal Conservatoire The Hague\, supp
 orted by CIIIC and Stimuleringsfonds.\n\nOrganisation: Futures of Listenin
 g (FIBER\, 4DSOUND\, Robin Koek\, Art of Sound)\nLocation: Amsterdam\, Net
 herlands\, with work at the 4DSOUND studio.\nAward: Total residency fee of
  EUR 7\,125\, calculated as 25 commissioned days at a day rate of EUR 285.
  Six of those 25 days can be spent at the 4DSOUND studio working with thei
 r team. Some additional financial support is available if needed\, includi
 ng material and travel costs\, but these must be clearly defined and agree
 d before the residency starts. No application fee.\nDuration: December 202
 6 to February 2027\, structured as 25 commissioned days. Deadline 13 Septe
 mber 2026.\n\nMore: https://fiber.homerun.co/artist-residency-architecture
 -on-sound/en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fiber.homerun.co/artist-residency-architecture-on-sound/en?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, Netherlands\, with work at the 4DSOUND studio.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:futures-of-listening-worlding-narratives-roaming-sound-space-2027@artif
 icialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: Futures of Listening: Worlding Narratives\, Roaming Sound
  Space Residency
DESCRIPTION:One residency to research and develop an interactive listening 
 experience built on non-linear sound narratives\, experienced by navigatin
 g through a series of virtual spaces or layers. NO VISUALS: Worlding Narra
 tives centres sound as the primary medium for immersion and intentionally 
 removes dominant visual layers such as VR\, AR\, projection or video. THE 
 DESIGN PROBLEM they want tackled is translation and adaptation\, specifica
 lly the shift from one visitor in a headphone-mediated experience to rende
 ring for a multi-speaker system for group interaction. That change in dyna
 mics\, reproduction and perspective is integral to the residency scope. RE
 SEARCH QUESTIONS include how immersive sound can function as a primary nar
 rative medium across speculative and non-fictional realities\, what new na
 rrative structures and dramaturgical methods become possible when the crea
 tive process originates from sound rather than adapting frameworks from ot
 her media\, and how interactive sonic structures can create navigable list
 ening experiences designed for and by multiple intelligences. Outcomes may
  include interactive sonic prototypes\, spatial audio compositions\, immer
 sive listening experiences\, narrative sound works or software prototypes.
  WORTH NOTING: your residency runs in tandem with resident Pinar Temiz\, a
 n expert in sound design for gaming environments\, with the opportunity to
  work together. Lead researcher is Dr Angela McArthur of UCL\, with resear
 ch support from Dr meLe yamomo of the University of Amsterdam. WHO: media 
 and sound artists\, sound designers\, musicians producing their own sonic 
 work\, field recordists\, writers\, composers and game sound designers. Ex
 perience with interactive audio\, spatial sound tools or game-sound workfl
 ows is welcome but not required. HARD ELIGIBILITY GATE: applicants must be
  based in the Netherlands AND registered as an artist with the Dutch Chamb
 er of Commerce (KvK). This is not negotiable and rules out non-NL applican
 ts. Futures of Listening is a Netherlands-based platform for spatial sound
 \, immersive experience\, performance and installation art\, founded by FI
 BER Festival\, 4DSOUND\, Robin Koek and Art of Sound at the Royal Conserva
 toire The Hague\, supported by CIIIC and Stimuleringsfonds.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Futures of Listening (FIBER\, 4DSOUND\, Robin Koek\, Art of Sound)\nLoc
 ation: Amsterdam\, Netherlands\, with remote and studio access to the 4DSO
 UND infrastructure.\nAward: Total residency fee of EUR 7\,125\, calculated
  as 25 commissioned days at a day rate of EUR 285. Six of those 25 days ca
